# --- OpenBox desktop (minimal, no display manager, no panel) --------------
# KDE Plasma was REMOVED (it did not fit the distro). OpenBox is now the whole
# desktop: a lightweight X11 window manager the startx session execs directly
# (exec openbox-session in ~/.xinitrc). There is NO panel -- the Az'arch
# application menu (Super key / centered popup) is the only shell surface, so no
# tint2/panel package is shipped. `xcape` turns a lone Super tap into Super+Menu
# so OpenBox's rc.xml can bind the menu launcher to the bare Super key (OpenBox
# cannot bind a lone modifier itself). `feh` (already in the manifest) paints the
# wallpaper from the OpenBox autostart. kitty is the ONE terminal (bound to W-Return
# and seeded in the menu); xterm/uxterm are deliberately NOT shipped -- the `xterm`
# package drags in both and the user does not want them. No sddm (autologin + startx).
openbox
xcape
adwaita-icon-theme
gnome-themes-extra
xcursor-themes
# --- Calamares installer dependencies -------------------------------------
# The graphical installer (built via makepkg, see configuration/pkgbuild.py) is a
# Qt6/KDE-Frameworks app: `pacman -Si calamares` depends on kcrash kconfig
# kcoreaddons kiconthemes ki18n kpmcore polkit-qt6 qt6-svg solid yaml-cpp (+ the
# ckbcomp/hwinfo/squashfs-tools already present). These K* + Qt6 packages therefore
# STAY even though Plasma is gone -- they are the installer's toolkit, not the
# desktop shell. qt6-declarative/qt6-5compat back Calamares' QML pages.
kpmcore
qt6-base
qt6-svg
qt6-declarative
qt6-5compat
kconfig
kcoreaddons
ki18n
kcrash
kwidgetsaddons
kiconthemes
kpackage
yaml-cpp
polkit
polkit-qt6
