# firefox: shipped ALONGSIDE LibreWolf so it is a real, always-present choice in
# `azarch default-applications` (the user: "I have firefox installed, but i dont see it").
# With firefox in the image, firefox.desktop always exists, so the Web/HTML/PDF quick-picks
# that offer it (default_applications.CANDIDATES) always resolve. LibreWolf stays the shipped
# DEFAULT; firefox is just available to switch to.
firefox
gedit
gimp
# --- Thunar file manager (GTK, replaces Dolphin) --------------------------
# Dolphin (KDE/KF6) was DROPPED: too many Az'arch tweaks required fighting hardcoded
# C++ strings, QRC templates and KIOSK lockdowns. Thunar (Xfce's GTK file manager) is
# the better fit -- it matches the rest of the GTK desktop (gedit/gimp/xviewer + the
# Adwaita theme + the QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=gtk3 bridge), is minimal and stable, and its
# custom right-click actions (~/.config/Thunar/uca.xml) are a first-class feature that
# runs any command with mime/pattern conditions -- exactly what the "Create Link" and
# "Edit with gedit/gimp" requirements need. Configured by modifications/thunar/.
thunar
# thunar-volman: removable-media handling (auto-mount/auto-run of USB drives, discs).
# Thunar's "Removable drives and media" is this plugin; without it Thunar cannot manage
# hotplugged volumes. (Its extra Settings launcher is suppressed in the app menu.)
thunar-volman
# thunar-archive-plugin: "Extract Here" / "Create Archive" right-click entries, backed by
# file-roller (already pulled in). Makes archives first-class in the context menu.
thunar-archive-plugin
# tumbler: the thumbnail service Thunar calls to render image/video/PDF thumbnails in the
# icon view. Without it Thunar shows generic icons instead of previews.
tumbler
# zenity: GTK dialog helper. The "Create Link" custom action prompts for a name + target
# via zenity (GTK, fits the desktop better than kdialog). Also generally useful for
# shell-driven GUI prompts.
zenity
# exo: provides exo-open, the Xfce "preferred applications" launcher Thunar's default
# "Open Terminal Here" uses (`exo-open --launch TerminalEmulator`). Az'arch points the
# preferred TerminalEmulator at kitty (packages/azarch/default_applications.py).
exo
# --- xviewer (the "Photos" default image viewer, GTK) ---------------------
# The XDG "Photos"/image default (Default Applications maps image/* to it). Ships with an
# off-putting "spying eye" icon that modifications/xviewer.py replaces with an Az'arch icon.
xviewer
qalculate-gtk
